<title>USA: KOCH raises U.S. posted crude prices 75 cts/bbl.</title>
<headline>KOCH raises U.S. posted crude prices 75 cts/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 75 cents a barrel across the board, effective Nov 13.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $22.50 a barrel.</p>
<p>West Texas Sour is up to $20.25 a barrel, Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $22.50 a barrel and Oklahoma sweet is $22.50.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
